From 6d0597910edb814cfb28206739282a1c11080caf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritesh Pandit <riteshp2001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:10:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 135/140] fix: enable nested swipes and avoid redundant folder
 refreshes

Music, Network, and Recents gestures
- Add an explicit nested-swipe opt-in to NavigationPager and enable it for
  Music, Network, and Recents Audio/Video tabs. Leave other nested pagers
  unchanged and retain existing tab identity, selection, and scroll state.
- Enable local song and audio-folder list swipe actions using the existing
  configurable left/right actions, thresholds, feedback, and accessibility
  behavior. Reuse the shared gesture surface rather than add another engine.
- Keep middle-of-row gestures available for tab changes, with item actions
  on edge-origin drags. Preserve grid and multi-selection restrictions.
- Add optional swipe support to the shared music row and wire the Songs
  list to existing queue, playlist, delete, and playback-mark handlers.
- Collect only audio files for Music folder actions, retain video-only
  collection elsewhere, and preserve recursive scope, symlink exclusions,
  cancellation, and destructive-action confirmations.
- Mark collected audio correctly for audio playlists and use target-aware
  delete labels. Translate new audio confirmations/loading/empty states
  and the shared swipe-settings title in all ten resource sets.

Folder NEW indicator refresh
- Remove the folder screen's ON_RESUME badge-recalculation callback, which
  was replayed when tab content re-entered composition.
- Keep one view-model-owned, debounced collector for folder data, badge
  preferences, and playback-state events, independent of tab visibility.
- Cache folder media membership for badge-only updates and invalidate it
  on actual library loads/manual refresh even if folder metadata is equal.
- Rethrow cancellation and check job activity before caching/publishing so
  cancelled work cannot briefly replace the displayed indicators with zeros.

Skip pills and online subtitle search
- Do not publish a manual skip pill for segments configured for auto-skip:
  intro/recap use auto-intro, outro/credits/preview use auto-outro.
- Re-evaluate immediately on preference changes using the existing serial
  playback dispatcher. Keep pills hidden while paused too, without removing
  seekbar markers or changing the automatic seek policy.
- Restore online subtitle search's original inline reset/clear/AI/search
  controls, marquee, adjacent season controls, fixed search area, and
  separately scrolling results. Relative to the previous layout, retain
  only four padding changes, as requested.

Website contrast and Vercel previews
- Give dark hero-overlay badges explicit light foreground/icon colors so
  they remain readable when the website uses its light theme.
- Keep the existing master-only deployment policy and add an ignoreCommand
  that allows production builds without a pull-request ID, skipping other
  environments before installation/build. Android PR CI is unchanged.
- Vercel may still report a skipped/cancelled integration status; this guard
  prevents preview builds, not the existence of a GitHub status entry.

Validation and scope
- Focused editor diagnostics, source/call-site and diff inspection, JSON/XML
  parsing, localized format-argument checks, and git diff --check passed.
  Refreshed the static source graph.
- Per standing instructions, no Android/website builds, tests, formatter,
  emulator, device gestures/playback, browser screenshots, or live Vercel
  deployment checks were run. Compilation and runtime validation remain
  required; clean editor diagnostics are not compiler proof.
- Preserve the published player-sheet changes and visible-but-disabled
  empty chapter icons. No generated schemas or changelog files edited.
